Talus GIS is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3 (see LICENSE). This release also
includes, and its api image contains, software written by others under their own licenses:

* The browser application (web/dist) bundles open-source JavaScript packages and fonts. Their notices
  and license texts are in web/dist/third-party-licenses.txt, also shown in Talus under
  "Open-source licenses".

* The api image (ghcr.io/talusgis/talus-api) contains open-source software, some licensed under the
  GNU GPL and LGPL. Its complete notices are inside the image at /usr/share/doc/talus/NOTICES. The
  corresponding source code of its GPL and LGPL components is published with each release at
  https://github.com/TalusGIS/talus/releases.

* The datum correction files in api/datum_grids are the U.S. National Geodetic Survey's published grids
  (NAD27 to NAD83, and NAD83 to NAD83(HARN)), in the form the PROJ project distributes them. They are in
  the public domain; us_noaa_README.txt in that folder is the PROJ project's description of each.

* db/proj/proj.db is the reference database of the PROJ coordinate library (MIT license), as distributed in
  the database image named in docker-compose.yml. It contains the EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset, which is
  owned by IOGP (the International Association of Oil and Gas Producers) and is used under its terms of use,
  https://epsg.org/terms-of-use.html. Talus has changed three records in it: the operations "NAD83(HARN) to
  WGS 84 (2)" and "(3)" and "NAD83(CSRS) to WGS 84 (2)" (EPSG codes 1900, 1901 and 1946) are marked
  deprecated; those three records are not EPSG's data as published. Every other record is unchanged.
  db/proj/README.md says why. The api image carries the same change in its own copies, under the same
  terms.

* The other images named in docker-compose.yml (PostgreSQL/PostGIS, Keycloak, OpenFGA, Caddy,
  pg_tileserv, Flyway, curl) are not part of this release. Docker pulls them from their publishers,
  under their publishers' licenses.
